{
  "name": "swim_back",
  "//": "SWIMMING BACKWARD (moving against the facing): upright, leaning back 15 degrees. Both hands push the water away in front -- from the chest out to straight arms, then sweep out to the sides and fold back in -- while the legs pedal forward, the reverse of the tread's egg-beater. Rotations: hips = lean Z (+ = right) of pitch X (+ = forward) of roll Y; every other part = sweep Y of flex X of abduction Z. A hanging limb: X negative = forward/up, positive = back; Z negative = the RIGHT limb out from the side. Knees +X bend, elbows -X bend. Hips pos in decimetres. All six swim clips share one 1600 ms period and one playhead (pose.cpp, the swim family), so a blend of two directions strokes in step.",
